From: LukeValen <panvk-eden@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH csf-v11 111] panvk: quiet hot-path Eden diagnostics

The bring-up builds logged every Android release fence, every Kbase sync-file
export, and every Kbase BO lifetime transition. Those logs were useful while
isolating the crash, but they sit on presentation and allocation hot paths and
distort emulator performance.

Keep error/fatal diagnostics and CSF fault snapshots, but remove successful
per-frame/per-allocation info logging from normal Eden builds.

Target: Eden Android / Mali-G615 MC6 / Kbase CSF v11

diff --git a/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_android.c b/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_android.c
index de88bda..23c8d83 100644
